config BENCHMARK_BM2PID
	bool "bm2pid: 3-axis cascaded PID control benchmark"
	default n
	---help---
		K-Fusion BM2 benchmark: a realistic periodic control workload.

		Three axes, each with a cascaded position/velocity PID, integral
		anti-windup and an 8-tap FIR on the feedback signal.  Runs at 1 kHz
		with clock_nanosleep(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, TIMER_ABSTIME), exactly like
		cyclictest, so the jitter numbers are directly comparable.

		Unlike cyclictest it also reports:
		  - per-cycle execution time and overrun count (exec > period)
		  - control quality (mean-square and max tracking error)

		The control-quality numbers are what reveals a fixed-point
		conversion that changed numeric behaviour: jitter may look fine
		while the controller has silently diverged.

		The hot loop never prints; output happens once at the end.
